lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Patches for 3.3 M2 development =
are being tested and merged. We have one week left before M2 is due to =
be built.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l0 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>It was a mixed week for builds =
and patches, several reproducibility issues appeared and issues also =
appeared after patches had merged in the second or third build after =
that due to state reuse and differences between worker distros. This =
makes merging the patches challenging.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l0 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>In particular, an upgrade to =
qemu 5.2.0 did merge. That upgrade includes a change to the underlying =
build system and the patchset was significantly rationalised which may =
cause issues. In particular, issues on centos hosts were eventually =
traced to the mmap_min_addr setting being too low (65536 now seems to be =
the useful minimum).<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l0 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>We are now tracking =
intermittent ptest failures and a number of bugs have been opened for =
these, we don&#8217;t as yet have people able to work on them =
though.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l0 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>CVE metrics are starting to =
trend down again but we still have 56 &#8220;open&#8221; CVEs against =
master and more in gatesgath/dunfell so help in further reducing the =
number would be appreciated.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l0 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Intermittent autobuilder issues =
continue to occur and with more invasive changes and higher rebuild =
rates, the numbers are increasing again. You can see the list of =
failures we&#8217;re continuing to see by searching for the =
&#8220;AB-INT&#8221; tag in bugzilla: <a =
href=3D"https://bugzilla.yoctoproject.org/buglist.cgi?quicksearch=3DAB-IN=
